Give the game's view a root, for the in-game settings beside the on-screen controls.

The game's window held one view, AKHostView, as its controller's whole view. Brighter
Pocket's in-game settings (pocket/translation/AppKit/PocketSettings.m, added by the layer)
need room around it: a gear button beside the on-screen controls, a performance overlay, a
settings sheet, and a black border when the game's view is kept inside the safe area. The
controller's view is now a black root; PocketSettingsAttach puts the game's view in it,
inside the safe area or over the whole screen, and the settings above it. The window still
takes its size from AKHostView, so the game's window follows the border and the
orientation, as it followed the view before ("window content size -> WxH"). The controller
answers supportedInterfaceOrientations as the player chose. AKHostView lets the settings
find its on-screen controls, to put the button beside them, and show or remove them while
the game runs. Upstream candidate in a general form: a host root with a place for
per-app overlays; as it stands it names this layer's settings.

